# LeakSanitizer suppressions.
#
# Every entry here is known debt, not noise. If the cause gets fixed, drop the
# line: LSAN reports suppressions that stop matching.

# Token copies made by TSAVE (docsis_lex.l) that are lost when the parse
# aborts before reaching the encoder, which owns them.
#
# The encoders in docsis_encode.c free these strings on the normal path
# (~20 free(helper->strval) calls there), so an arena in the lexer would free
# them twice. Fixing this properly means unifying ownership across those 20
# sites, which also carries a documented landmine: the TODO at
# docsis_encode.c:656 about T_STRING values, which point at the static strbuf
# rather than at an allocated copy.
#
# Bound: a few bytes per failed parse, and only when the error happens after
# an IP, MAC, hex or OID token. Does not grow with successful parses.
leak:docsis_lex
